; Build-time setup: load the module via IPM (imports + compiles classes,
; creates the SPA web app, runs Setup.PostInstall → REST app + seed + embeddings).
zn "FAST"
zpm "load /home/irisowner/app -v"
; Start the real interoperability production AFTER the IPM load completes — it
; cannot start inside IPM's install transaction (<COMMAND> *NoTransaction).
do ##class(FAST.Runtime.Runtime).EnsureProduction()
; Re-run the demo working state now the production is up: the starter PA queue
; (place + submit two orders through the real pipeline, replaying the cached
; packets) could not run during the install. Idempotent for everything else.
do ##class(FAST.Seed.SeedLoader).SeedDemoState()
halt
